# Case: Independent Desktop role processes
# Mode: process
# Purpose: Normal runtime retains tray and service after GUI close and independently recreates GUI and quick-panel processes.
# Steps:
#   Start normal mode with explicit background intent, verify no initial GUI, reopen and close each UI role, then verify durable state and cleanup.
# Expected:
#   Tray, GUI, quick panel and unicd have independent process identities; tray activation works with unicd already running.
# Forbidden:
#   Resident hidden GUI, shared role PID, duplicate owners, foreign-profile activation, lost state, leaked processes, or native acceptance claims.

acceptance startup desktop-processes
